{"parentUuid":"4030902d-a0d9-4b8b-9637-916f91f05ef2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"acfa851c1bf88b5b3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013bka2H7Ckw3PM7ChfWvt4x","type":"tool_result","content":"data/seed-map.json:61:    \"physically based rendering\": [\"RND.MAT.model\", \"RND.LIGHT.units\", \"RND.POST.camera\"],\ndata/contracts.json:23:    {\"id\": \"C-IO\", \"layer\": 2, \"owner\": \"async-io-storage\", \"name\": \"Async IO\", \"summary\": \"IO requests, priorities, deadlines, completions, decompression targets.\", \"requires\": [\"C-PAL\", \"C-TASK\"]},\ndata/contracts.json:26:    {\"id\": \"C-RES\", \"layer\": 2, \"owner\": \"resource-streaming-architect\", \"name\": \"Resource lifetime & streaming requests\", \"summary\": \"Handles, request priority/deadline, residency callbacks, budgets, fallbacks.\", \"requires\": [\"C-ASSET\", \"C-VFS\", \"C-MEM\"]},\ndata/contracts.json:49:    {\"id\": \"C-NAV\", \"layer\": 3, \"owner\": \"navigation-pathfinding\", \"name\": \"Navigation queries\", \"summary\": \"Path requests, navmesh/grid queries, dynamic obstacles.\", \"requires\": [\"C-SPATIAL\", \"C-PHYS\"]},\ndata/contracts.json:62:    {\"id\": \"C-ORCH\", \"layer\": \"P\", \"owner\": \"program-orchestration\", \"name\": \"Agent coordination protocol\", \"summary\": \"Ownership ledger, change requests, integration order, critic gates.\", \"requires\": [], \"universal\": \"all\"},\ndata/capabilities.json:36:        [\"ARCH.ORG.change-requests\", \"Contract change-request protocol between agents\", \"program-orchestration\", \"E\", [\"architecture-governance\"]],\ndata/capabilities.json:197:        [\"RES.MGMT.requests\", \"Load requests with priority & deadline\", \"resource-streaming-architect\", \"E\"],\ndata/capabilities.json:276:        [\"WLD.SPACE.lwc\", \"Large-world coordinates implementation (64-bit positions, camera-relative)\", \"spatial-transforms\", \"E\"],\ndata/capabilities.json:288:        [\"WLD.ENV.wind\", \"Wind & interaction\", \"vegetation-foliage\", \"E\"],\ndata/capabilities.json:444:        [\"RND.POST.camera\", \"Physical camera & exposure\", \"post-color-hdr\", \"E\"],\ndata/capabilities.json:521:        [\"PHY.CTRL.platforms\", \"Moving platforms & physical interaction\", \"character-vehicle-physics\", \"E\"]\ndata/capabilities.json:597:        [\"ANM.CINE.cameras\", \"Camera cuts & cinematic cameras\", \"cinematics-sequencer\", \"E\"],\ndata/capabilities.json:718:        [\"GAM.SYS.camera\", \"Camera system (rigs, blending, collision)\", \"gameplay-systems-toolkit\", \"E\"],\ndata/capabilities.json:731:        [\"GAM.SCR.gc\", \"Garbage-collection policy & engine interaction\", \"scripting-runtime\", \"E\"]\ndata/capabilities.json:821:        [\"ED.WORLD.viewport\", \"Viewport & camera navigation\", \"world-editor-viewport\", \"E\"],\ndata/skills.json:39:     \"purpose\": \"Turns architecture into coordinated multi-agent work: decomposes milestones into tasks by skill territory, keeps the ownership ledger and territory locks, sequences integration through vertical slices, routes contract change requests, and schedules critic gates.\",\ndata/skills.json:231:     \"purpose\": \"Runtime resource model: handles and explicit lifetime, load requests with priority and deadline, dependency-aware loading, the streaming manager (budgets, eviction, prediction), fallbacks, no-stall loading.\",\ndata/skills.json:260:     \"purpose\": \"Vegetation instancing and rendering, procedural placement rules, wind and interaction, vegetation-specific LOD.\",\ndata/skills.json:333:     \"purpose\": \"Post chain, physical camera and exposure, end-to-end color management (working space, output transforms, OCIO), HDR output and calibration, tonemapping, grading.\",\ndata/skills.json:366:     \"purpose\": \"Character controllers (kinematic and dynamic), vehicles (wheels, tires, suspension, drivetrain), buoyancy, moving platforms and physical interaction.\",\ndata/skills.json:415:     \"purpose\": \"Timeline/sequencer, camera cuts and cinematic cameras, high-quality movie rendering, cutscene streaming and preloading.\",\ndata/skills.json:416:     \"non_responsibilities\": [[\"Gameplay camera\", \"gameplay-systems-toolkit\"], [\"Path tracer\", \"path-tracing\"]],\ndata/skills.json:459:     \"non_responsibilities\": [[\"Abilities/tags/camera toolkit\", \"gameplay-systems-toolkit\"], [\"Scripting VM\", \"scripting-runtime\"], [\"Game-specific code (the game team)\", \"engine-architect\"]],\ndata/skills.json:462:     \"purpose\": \"Reusable gameplay systems: abilities, effects and attributes, gameplay tags, camera system, spawning and pooling, gameplay message routing, photo mode.\",\ndata/skills.json:463:     \"non_responsibilities\": [[\"Generic events\", \"entity-object-model\"], [\"Cinematic cameras\", \"cinematics-sequencer\"]],\ndata/skills.json:464:     \"provides\": [], \"consumes\": [\"C-GAME\", \"C-NET?\", \"C-INPUT?\"], \"expertise\": [\"ability systems\", \"camera design\", \"gameplay tags\"]},\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:36:- **Change control.** Contract changes go through the change-request protocol (`C-ORCH`), so parallel agents cannot silently break each other.\ndocs/00-design-principles.md:99:- **Technique selection inside a skill.** For example, archetype vs sparse-set ECS, or virtual shadow maps vs ray-traced shadows as the default. Those are phase-2 SKILL.md content and implementation-time ADRs. Phase 1 only guarantees that each question has exactly one owner and that the alternatives are visible (see `06-gap-analysis.md`).\ndocs/04-cross-cutting.md:35:- **program-orchestration** (orchestrator) — Turns architecture into coordinated multi-agent work: decomposes milestones into tasks by skill territory, keeps the ownership ledger and territory locks, sequences integration through vertical slices, routes contract change requests, and schedules critic gates.\n00-design-principles.md\n01-capability-map.md\n02-skill-dependency-graph.md\n03-skill-hierarchy.md\n04-cross-cutting.md\n05-critic-framework.md\n06-gap-analysis.md\n07-research-plan.md\n08-phase-2-plan.md\n226\n{\"_doc\": \"Every domain term named in the mission brief, mapped to the capabilities that cover it. The checker fails if any term maps to nothing or to an unknown capability. Adding a term here is how a critic's 'missing X' becomes a machine-checked obligation.\", \"brief_domains\": {\"engine architecture\": [\"ARCH.STRUCT.layering\", \"ARCH.STRUCT.contracts\"], \"platform abstraction\": [\"PLAT.PAL.os\"], \"hardware abstraction\": [\"PLAT.PAL.cpu-topology\", \"RND.RHI.backends\", \"RND.RHI.caps\"], \"core runtime\": [\"CORE.LIFE.boot\", \"CORE.LIFE.modules\"], \"memory management\": [\"CORE.MEM.virtual\", \"CORE.MEM.oom\"], \"allocators\": [\"CORE.MEM.allocators\"], \"containers\": [\"CORE.TYPES.containers\"], \"concurrency\": [\"CORE.CONC.sync\", \"CORE.JOBS.scheduler\"], \"synchronization\": [\"CORE.CONC.sync\", \"RND.RHI.sync\"], \"atomics\": [\"CORE.CONC.atomics\"], \"lock-free structures\": [\"CORE.CONC.lockfree\", \"CORE.CONC.reclamation\"], \"job systems\": [\"CORE.JOBS.scheduler\"], \"task graphs\": [\"CORE.JOBS.graph\"], \"fibers/coroutines\": [\"CORE.JOBS.fibers\"], \"ECS\": [\"CORE.ECS.storage\", \"CORE.ECS.queries\"], \"object/entity identity\": [\"CORE.OBJ.identity\"], \"reflection\": [\"CORE.REFL.registry\"], \"metadata\": [\"CORE.REFL.attributes\"], \"serialization\": [\"CORE.SER.binary\", \"CORE.SER.evolution\"], \"configuration\": [\"CORE.LIFE.config\"], \"logging\": [\"OBS.LOG.logging\"], \"diagnostics\": [\"OBS.LOG.remote\", \"OBS.CRASH.hangs\"], \"crash handling\": [\"OBS.CRASH.capture\", \"OBS.CRASH.pipeline\"], \"telemetry\": [\"OBS.LOG.telemetry\"], \"profiling\": [\"OBS.LOG.tr","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"452396f5-f8c0-4c64-b3bd-49307ca11014","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:52:07.686Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4030902d-a0d9-4b8b-9637-916f91f05ef2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
